hw/ - FPGA hardware for the UART-attached CGRA
==============================================

VHDL-2008 for an R x C mesh of 16-bit processing elements (default 4x4,
legacy device protocol up to 16 PEs), UART and protocol-v3 controller.
Simulate with GHDL; synthesize and implement with Vivado batch mode.

Boards
------
    nexys_a7    Nexys 4 DDR / Nexys A7-100T, xc7a100tcsg324-1 (default)
    basys3      Basys 3, xc7a35tcpg236-1
Both board constraints assume a 100 MHz physical oscillator. PERIOD changes
only the timing constraint, never the oscillator or UART baud generator.

Layout
------
    rtl/        production VHDL
    sim/        GHDL testbenches and C differential vector generators
    formal/     executable production RTL properties, contract and runner
    con/        physical pin, I/O standard and configuration constraints
    scr/        Vivado flows, timing/structural checks and artifact runner
    test/       offline flow/publication regression tests (not Vivado evidence)
    perf/       historical Fmax trajectory; new measurements are per-run

Commands (from hw/; make -f hw.mk TARGET)
----------------------------------------
    sim             all GHDL regressions
    lint            analyze production RTL
    wave            top-level testbench, build/tb_cgra_top.ghw
    test-scripts    Tcl flow decisions and Python artifact regressions
    formal-fast     required production PE/controller and selected RTL proofs
    formal-full     extended instances and mutation checks
    formal-cover    reachability, separately labelled from universal proofs
    synth           synthesis and structural/constraint checks; no routing
    sta             synthesis, placement, route and physical gates
    bit             same physical gates, then bitstream generation
    fmax            period search, followed by final route and physical gates
    check-artifact  validate an explicit ARTIFACT manifest without hardware
    prog            program selected artifact through Vivado hardware server
    prog-ofl        program selected artifact through openFPGALoader

Knobs: BOARD, MESH_ROWS, MESH_COLS, STEP_DIV, PERIOD, FLOORPLAN=1, VIVADO.
Programming requires ARTIFACT=/path/to/a/successful/bit-run/manifest.json.
Board, geometry and STEP_DIV must match; loose .bit files are not accepted.
For an alternate part, pass BOARD explicitly, including during programming.

Artifacts and guarantees
------------------------
Every Make physical run gets a fresh build/vivado/runs/MODE-ID directory
with input copies, manifest, reports and tool log. Success updates a small
pointer under build/vivado/current/. Failure retains its evidence and leaves
the previous valid pointer intact. The manifest binds hashes of RTL, scripts,
constraints, reports/checkpoints and bitstream to the actual parameters/tool.
Read ../doc/physical-flow.md for the schema, gates and known limits.

The datapath advances on a clock enable. STEP_DIV drives both the RTL generic
and setup/hold multicycle factors. Constraints enumerate every register bit;
only the PE D endpoints receive the exception. CE/reset remain single-cycle.
Formal controller proofs check reset/first-step guard, spacing and CFG/WR to
capture guard for the documented instances. Real Vivado checks the selected
pins and actual timing requirements. Synchronizer ASYNC_REG preservation,
first-stage fanout and pair placement are checked on the implemented netlist.

STA establishes slack under the applied model/constraints. It does not prove
that a bitstream works on a board, certify analog metastability, or measure
serial throughput. A clean synthesis is distinct from a routed timing pass;
both are distinct from physical device tests. PERIOD>10 ns may be explored by
sta/fmax, but cannot qualify a programmable artifact for these 100 MHz boards.

Wire contract
-------------
RTL constants in rtl/cgra_pkg.vhd align with ../lib/include/cgra.h and the
C model. Legacy CFG/WR can partially update registers before a NACK; rejection
is not rollback. The clockless C model does not model the temporal watchdog.
